[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ast-grep could match sdoc files directly using the grammar we already package

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-ASTGREP-OVER-SDOC
TITLE: ast-grep could match sdoc files directly using the grammar we already package
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
ast-grep is tree-sitter based and takes custom languages through a dynamic
tree-sitter library. This repository already packages a patched
tree-sitter-strictdoc for semble, so the grammar half of that already exists
and is already maintained.

That makes structural matching over sdoc documents available without writing a
parser: find every node carrying a given field value, rewrite a field across a
corpus, lint for a shape the strictdoc grammar cannot express. Relevant to the
milestone that makes a tool the only writer of sdoc files, where the
alternative is driving strictdoc's own node model for every edit.

Unproven. Registering a custom language with ast-grep needs the grammar built
as a shared library with the right entry point, which the semble packaging may
or may not already produce.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Noted while measuring ast-grep for the grammar milestone's conversion pass.
Two capabilities this repository already carries separately turn out to
compose, and nothing records that they might.
<<<
